ecursing source+body, and setting flags for sort_by/max_by.\n4. expr arms.\n\nLet me design JS helpers:\n\n```js\nfunction tl_sort_by(src, f) {\n  const keys = src.map(f);\n  const idx = [...src.keys()].sort((a, b) => keys[a] < keys[b] ? -1 : keys[a] > keys[b] ? 1 : 0);\n  return idx.map((i) => src[i]);\n}\n```\n\nHmm — for Str keys, JS `<`/`>` on strings mis-orders astral chars (as discussed). So I need a comparator for Str keys: `tl_str_cmp`. And for Char — Char is a number in JS? Let me check JS's Char type. Let me grep.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_068ea2156001KlshSgvs0336pd","sessionID":"ses_f971d285effeq84jbpOgeGh3gS","messageID":"msg_068ea149b001BJKHZMY7TzySSC"}}
