{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788466682897,"sessionID":"ses_f971d285effeq84jbpOgeGh3gS","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_d06b74868f984f26809dc2bc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/runtime/toylang.c","limit":70,"offset":1070},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/runtime/toylang.c</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1070: }\n1071: \n1072: /* Split every line of a Vec<Str> on the delimiter, one row per line: `dsv(delim)`. The outer\n1073:  * Vec is a single column of inner Vecs, the struct-of-arrays spelling of Vec<Vec<Str>>. */\n1074: tl_vec *tl_split_lines(tl_vec *lines, tl_str *sep) {\n1075:     tl_vec *out = tl_vec_new(lines->len, 1);\n1076:     for (int64_t i = 0; i < lines->len; i++) {\n1077:         out->cols[0][i] = (int64_t)tl_split((tl_str *)lines->cols[0][i], sep);\n1078:     }\n1079:     return out;\n1080: }\n1081: \n1082: /* Gather one element of a Vec of records back into a record.\n1083:  *\n1084:  * The struct-of-arrays layout means an element is spread across columns, and almost nothing in\n1085:  * the language needs it whole: select reads single fields out of the columns, and `.field`\n1086:  * returns a column. Printing is the exception, because rendering an element needs every field\n1087:  * at once. This is the only gather, and it exists for output alone.\n1088:  */\n1089: int64_t *tl_rec_from_vec(const tl_vec *v, int64_t i) {\n1090:     int64_t *rec = tl_rec_new(v->ncols);\n1091:     for (int64_t c = 0; c < v->ncols; c++) {\n1092:         rec[c] = v->cols[c][i];\n1093:     }\n1094:     return rec;\n1095: }\n1096: \n1097: /* Opt: a pointer to a slot, or NULL for absent.\n1098:  *\n1099:  * Boxing rather than a tag pair, because a slot holds any value an Int can and there is no\n1100:  * spare bit pattern to mean absent. Uniform across element types, which is what lets one\n1101:  * function serve them all.\n1102:  */\n1103: int64_t *tl_opt_some(int64_t value) {\n1104:     int64_t *p = tl_alloc(sizeof(int64_t));\n1105:     *p = value;\n1106:     return p;\n1107: }\n1108: \n1109: int64_t tl_opt_is_some(const int64_t *o) {\n1110:     return o != NULL;\n1111: }\n1112: \n1113: int64_t tl_opt_get(const int64_t *o) {\n1114:     return *o;\n1115: }\n1116: \n1117: /* Every element but the first. NULL on an empty Vec -- the same absence encoding tl_opt_some\n1118:  * uses everywhere else, so a caller unwraps it the same way an Index result is unwrapped. */\n1119: int64_t *tl_vec_tail(const tl_vec *v) {\n1120:     if (v->len == 0) {\n1121:         return NULL;\n1122:     }\n1123:     tl_vec *out = tl_vec_new(v->len - 1, v->ncols);\n1124:     for (int64_t c = 0; c < v->ncols; c++) {\n1125:         if (out->len > 0) {\n1126:             memcpy(out->cols[c], v->cols[c] + 1, (size_t)out->len * sizeof(int64_t));\n1127:         }\n1128:     }\n1129:     return tl_opt_some((int64_t)out);\n1130: }\n1131: \n1132: /* Flatten a Vec<Vec<T>> into a Vec<T>. `ncols` is T's column count: passed in rather than read\n1133:  * off an inner Vec, since an empty outer Vec has no inner Vec to read it from. */\n1134: tl_vec *tl_vec_flatten(const tl_vec *vv, int64_t ncols) {\n1135:     int64_t total = 0;\n1136:     for (int64_t i = 0; i < vv->len; i++) {\n1137:         total += ((const tl_vec *)vv->cols[0][i])->len;\n1138:     }\n1139:     tl_vec *out = tl_vec_new(total, ncols);\n\n(Showing lines 1070-1139 of 1405. Use offset=1140 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"}\n\n/* Split every line of a Vec<Str> on the delimiter, one row per line: `dsv(delim)`. The outer\n * Vec is a single column of inner Vecs, the struct-of-arrays spelling of Vec<Vec<Str>>. */\ntl_vec *tl_split_lines(tl_vec *lines, tl_str *sep) {\n    tl_vec *out = tl_vec_new(lines->len, 1);\n    for (int64_t i = 0; i < lines->len; i++) {\n        out->cols[0][i] = (int64_t)tl_split((tl_str *)lines->cols[0][i], sep);\n    }\n    return out;\n}\n\n/* Gather one element of a Vec of records back into a record.\n *\n * The struct-of-arrays layout means an element is spread across columns, and almost nothing in\n * the language needs it whole: select reads single fields out of the columns, and `.field`\n * returns a column. Printing is the exception, because rendering an element needs every field\n * at once. This is the only gather, and it exists for output alone.\n */\nint64_t *tl_rec_from_vec(const tl_vec *v, int64_t i) {","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-177/runtime/toylang.c","text":"}\n\n/* Split every line of a Vec<Str> on the delimiter, one row per line: `dsv(delim)`. The outer\n * Vec is a single column of inner Vecs, the struct-of-arrays spelling of Vec<Vec<Str>>. */\ntl_vec *tl_split_lines(tl_vec *lines, tl_str *sep) {\n    tl_vec *out = tl_vec_new(lines->len, 1);\n    for (int64_t i = 0; i < lines->len; i++) {\n        out->cols[0][i] = (int64_t)tl_split((tl_str *)lines->cols[0][i], sep);\n    }\n    return out;\n}\n\n/* Gather one element of a Vec of records back into a record.\n *\n * The struct-of-arrays layout means an element is spread across columns, and almost nothing in\n * the language needs it whole: select reads single fields out of the columns, and `.field`\n * returns a column. Printing is the exception, because rendering an element needs every field\n * at once. This is the only gather, and it exists for output alone.\n */\nint64_t *tl_rec_from_vec(const tl_vec *v, int64_t i) {\n    int64_t *rec = tl_rec_new(v->ncols);\n    for (int64_t c = 0; c < v->ncols; c++) {\n        rec[c] = v->cols[c][i];\n    }\n    return rec;\n}\n\n/* Opt: a pointer to a slot, or NULL for absent.\n *\n * Boxing rather than a tag pair, because a slot holds any value an Int can and there is no\n * spare bit pattern to mean absent. Uniform across element types, which is what lets one\n * function serve them all.\n */\nint64_t *tl_opt_some(int64_t value) {\n    int64_t *p = tl_alloc(sizeof(int64_t));\n    *p = value;\n    return p;\n}\n\nint64_t tl_opt_is_some(const int64_t *o) {\n    return o != NULL;\n}\n\nint64_t tl_opt_get(const int64_t *o) {\n    return *o;\n}\n\n/* Every element but the first. NULL on an empty Vec -- the same absence encoding tl_opt_some\n * uses everywhere else, so a caller unwraps it the same way an Index result is unwrapped. */\nint64_t *tl_vec_tail(const tl_vec *v) {\n    if (v->len == 0) {\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    tl_vec *out = tl_vec_new(v->len - 1, v->ncols);\n    for (int64_t c = 0; c < v->ncols; c++) {\n        if (out->len > 0) {\n            memcpy(out->cols[c], v->cols[c] + 1, (size_t)out->len * sizeof(int64_t));\n        }\n    }\n    return tl_opt_some((int64_t)out);\n}\n\n/* Flatten a Vec<Vec<T>> into a Vec<T>. `ncols` is T's column count: passed in rather than read\n * off an inner Vec, since an empty outer Vec has no inner Vec to read it from. */\ntl_vec *tl_vec_flatten(const tl_vec *vv, int64_t ncols) {\n    int64_t total = 0;\n    for (int64_t i = 0; i < vv->len; i++) {\n        total += ((const tl_vec *)vv->cols[0][i])->len;\n    }\n    tl_vec *out = tl_vec_new(total, ncols);","lineStart":1070,"lineEnd":1139,"totalLines":1405,"truncated":true}},"title":"runtime/toylang.c","time":{"start":1788466682885,"end":1788466682895}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_068ebdbfb0010b4fDMCvjm1eqF","sessionID":"ses_f971d285effeq84jbpOgeGh3gS","messageID":"msg_068ebd64b001UzcqWVH9TrRZPC"}}
